   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Federation of Trade Unions of Kyrgyzstan (FTUKG) adopted a new communication strategy in January 2023 to promote formalization of the informal economy.

The strategy included:
&#x2022;	A new website (www.fpk.kg) with a dedicated section for workers in the informal economy.
&#x2022;	An information campaign (video-reels promoting decent work for the reduction of informal employment developed and broadcasted nationally; articles on the position of FTUKG on informal employment situation and platform employment published in newspapers and on social media platforms).
&#x2022;	A model collective agreement validated and adopted by the FTUKG for its affiliated sectorial trade unions that focuses on preventing and minimizing informal employment.
&#x2022;	Alliances with civil society organizations to jointly promote formalization.

From October 2022 to January 2023, six affiliates of the FTUKG (the Textile workers trade union; the Commerce and Food processing workers trade union; the Utilities sector workers trade union; the Transport workers trade union; the Metalworkers and Miners trade union; and the Construction workers trade union) developed individual strategic plans on formalizing informal employment. This included approaches on how to organize and integrate workers in the informal economy into trade unions in their respective sectors. The strategy plans were validated and approved by their respective General Councils. The ILO provided support through several capacity building events, including with support of RBSA contribution: 

&#x2022;	A two-day seminar for the FTUKG leaders and senior staff members on advocating for effective social protection system that would cover all workers (March 2022).
&#x2022;	A two-day training for the leaders and senior staff members of the FTUKG on strategic planning by applying foresight methodology (May 2022).
&#x2022;	A two-day seminar for the FTUKG leadership &#x201c;Workers&apos; organizations and the future of informal economy: Organizing the Informal Economy in Trade Unions&#x201d; (July 2022).
&#x2022;	A two-day sub-regional seminar on the role of Decent Work in ensuring lasting Peace and sustainable economic development (July 2022) with the participation of the FTUKG leaders. 
&#x2022;	A regional conference of trade unions of central Asian countries &quot;Trade unions role in harnessing digital transformations for labour market development and securing Decent Work&quot; (October 2022). 
&#x2022;	A workshop &quot;Gender-responsive diagnostics of the scope, incidence and drivers of the informal economy and employment in the Kyrgyz Republic&quot; (November 2022).
&#x2022;	Training on strategic planning for the transition from the informal to the formal economy (December 2022).
&#x2022;	A technical working meeting with the FTUKG and its affiliated trade unions to validate the results of the analysis of the collective bargaining agreements (January 2023).</narrative>
   </description>
